---
/**
 * The back office frame — `E10-55`.
 *
 * The prototype's shell, which the first build of these screens never adopted: a **persistent
 * sidebar** with four labelled groups and live counts, a header carrying a **title and a
 * subtitle**, and a mount point for **drawer** editing on any screen that edits.
 *
 * Andy: *"Shell first, then migrate screens into it."* So every back-office page becomes
 * `<BackofficeShell title=… subtitle=…>` wrapping its own body, and nothing else decides its
 * frame.
 *
 * ## The sidebar renders empty and is **built** by the client — `E10-73`
 *
 * The site is static, so the server cannot know which grants the reader holds. This used to ship
 * every link with `hidden` and let `shell.ts` remove the attribute from the ones the grants
 * allowed, which is fine for the reader and wrong for the document: **every route, its label and
 * the grants it requires were in the HTML of every back-office page**, and these pages are served
 * to anyone who asks for them. `view-source` was a complete map of the back office, no account
 * required — the same disclosure Andy objected to on `/dashboard`, one layer down and available
 * without even signing in.
 *
 * So the rail ships **empty** and `shell.ts` creates the links the reader may actually use. A
 * link that is visible but refuses on click is still worse than one that was never offered; now
 * neither exists.
 *
 * The route table itself is in the page's JavaScript, because a static site has to route in the
 * browser. That is a genuinely weaker hiding place than a server would give us and it is the
 * honest limit of this: a minified bundle is not a secret. It is still the difference between
 * reading the markup and reverse-engineering a chunk.
 *
 * ## Counts are a promise, so they are opt-in per item
 *
 * The prototype shows open orders on Today, blocking dishes on Dishes, and schools that cannot
 * trade on Schools. A count that is stale or wrong is worse than no count, so an item only gets
 * one when a page can supply it — `setNavCount()` — rather than every item rendering a zero that
 * may or may not mean anything.
 */
interface Props {
  /** The route this page is, so the sidebar can mark it current. */
  current: string;
  title: string;
  /** The line under the title. Every prototype screen has one; no live screen did. */
  subtitle: string;
}

const { current, title, subtitle } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="bo">
  <nav class="bo__nav" aria-label="Back office" data-bonav data-nav-current={current}>
    <!--
      The real mark, not a lime square.

      `logo-white.webp` is the variant for a dark ground and the sidebar is the darkest surface in
      the product; `logo.webp` is the one for light. The prototype drew a placeholder rectangle
      because it had no asset pipeline — copying the placeholder was reading the mock too literally,
      which is the same mistake as reading it too loosely.
    -->
    <a class="bo__brand" href="/dashboard" aria-label="GrayBag — back office home">
      <img src="/img/logo-white.webp" width="560" height="184" alt="GrayBag" />
    </a>

    <!--
      Empty on purpose. `shell.ts` fills it with the links this reader may use and nothing else —
      see the note above on why the list is not in the document.
    -->
    <div data-nav-rail></div>

    <!--
      Who is signed in, and as what. The old back office never said — you could be looking at a
      kitchen operator's view and a platform admin's and not be able to tell them apart.
    -->
    <p class="bo__who" data-nav-who hidden><b data-nav-email></b><span data-nav-role></span></p>
  </nav>

  <div class="bo__main">
    <header class="bo__top">
      <div>
        <h1 class="bo__title">{title}</h1>
        <p class="bo__sub" data-page-sub>{subtitle}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bo__spacer"></div>
      <slot name="actions" />
    </header>

    <div class="bo__scroll">
      <slot />
    </div>

    <!-- Drawer editing, available to any screen rather than only the dish workbench. -->
    <div class="bo__scrim" data-drawer-scrim hidden></div>
    <aside class="bo__drawer" data-drawer hidden role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="drawer-title">
      <header class="bo__drawer-head">
        <div>
          <h3 id="drawer-title" data-drawer-title>Edit</h3>
          <p class="sub" data-drawer-sub></p>
        </div>
        <div class="bo__spacer"></div>
        <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-drawer-close>Close</button>
      </header>
      <div class="bo__drawer-body" data-drawer-body></div>
      <div class="bo__drawer-foot" data-drawer-foot hidden></div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</div>
